for first test case
-------------------

Create an instance of Test Class--->@BeforeAll(can be non static)--->@BeforeEach--->Execute Test Case method with @Test--->@AfterEach---(After all test cases finished)--->@AfterAll(can be non static)


Second test case onwards: recursion type
------------------------

@BeforeAll<---(Run next Test case)---@AfterEach







@BeforeAll: runs once before all tests, usually for expensive setup that can be shared across all test cases like Db connection etc.


@BeforeEach: Runs before each test case, usually for setting fresh test data like creating new objects, adding some temp data in DB for testing etc.

@Test: actual test method

@AfterEach: Runs after each test case, to clean up the resource like close file, deleting temp data etc.

@AfterAll: runs once after all tests, clean up resources like closing DB connection etc.








