by default, test cases runs sequentially, but we can also set our test cases to run in parallel:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


from previous topic: Junit5 Architecture, its clear that, who helps test cases to run in parallel, its "PLATFORM LAUNCHER"







1st: calls discovery() method, and gets the TestPlan with Testcases hierarchy(engine wise)


This is the step, where parallelism strategy is used:
-----------------------------------------------------

2ndL calls execute() method of each test engine to get the test plan executed

public class Junit5LifecycleDemo {
	public Junit5LifecycleDemo(){
		System.out.println("Junit5LifecycleDemo class Instance created");
	}
	
	@BeforeAll
	static void beforeAll(){
		System.out.println("inside @BeforeAll method");
	}
	
	@BeforeEach
	void beforeEach(){
		System.out.println("inside @BeforeEach method");
	}
	
	@Test
	void testcaseA() throws InterruptedException{
		System.out.println("inside testcaseA, executed by:"+ Thread.currentThread().getName());
		Thread.sleep(1000);
		System.out.println("Finished testcaseA");
	}
	
	@Test
	void testcaseB() throws InterruptedException{
		System.out.println("inside testcaseA, executed by:"+ Thread.currentThread().getName());
		Thread.sleep(1000);
		System.out.println("Finished testcaseB");
	}
	
	@AfterEach
	void afterEach(){
		System.out.println("inside @AfterEach method");
	}
	
	@AfterAll
	static void afterAll(){
		System.out.println("inside @AfterAll method");
	}
	
}
	
	

/src/test/resources/junit-platform.properties
---------------------------------------------

#below configurations, junit platform launcher will apply to junit. jupiter(i.e Jupiter Test engine only)



#Enables or disables parallel execution, default value is "false"

junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.enabled=true


#Run methods within a test class in parallel, default value is "same_thread" mean sequentially

junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.mode.default=concurrent

#Multiple Test classes can be executed in parallel, default value is "same_thread" means sequentially

junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.mode.classes.default=concurrent



#thread pool managing strategy:

	# "dynamic" (default): thread pool size is computed dynamically based on system resources/junit-platform
	# "fixed" : we define the specific number of threads within a pool
	
junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.config.strategy=fixed



#used when "fixed" thread pool strategy is used, below it creates thread pool with 5 threads.

junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.config.fixed.parallelism=5
	
	
	









